# Dependencies and Tooling

## Ban

Do **not** add any third-party crate, crate.io package, Ada library, C library, or tool unless the user explicitly names it.

Do **not** vendor, wrap, or “temporarily” depend on wasm-tools, wit-bindgen, jco, cargo-component, or other Wasm toolchains unless the user says so. Lovelace implements binary/WIT/WAT emission itself.

## Allowed exceptions (only these)

1. **Wasmtime C library** — link **only** from crate `lovelace_jit` (`jit/`). Ada bindings in this repo. No Rust Wasmtime crates.
2. **AUnit** ([AdaCore/aunit](https://github.com/AdaCore/aunit)) — **required** for all tests.
3. **Git C library (libgit2)** — link **only** from crate `lovelace_hypatia` (`hypatia/`). Hand-written Ada `Interfaces.C` bindings in this repo. Used so Hypatia can clone/fetch git dependencies. No other Git wrappers or Ada git crates.
4. **GNATdoc** ([AdaCore/gnatdoc](https://github.com/AdaCore/gnatdoc), [Alire crate](https://alire.ada.dev/crates/gnatdoc)) — documentation generator only. Invoke via `scripts/gnatdoc.ps1`; do **not** `depends-on` it from library or `lovelace` crates.

Alire is the host build manager (one crate per component; see the Alire crates rule). Prefer declaring AUnit via Alire on **nested test crates** only; treat any other Alire crate as forbidden until the user approves it.

## Who may link what

- `lovelace_jit` — only crate that links `-lwasmtime` (or equivalent).
- `lovelace_hypatia` — only crate that links libgit2.
- Host tools (`lovelace_compiler`, `lovelace_lir`, `lovelace_common`, `lovelace`, `lovelace_jit`, `lovelace_tooling`, `lovelace_hypatia`, `lovelace_alexandria`, `lovelace_format`) may use the full GNAT runtime.
- Augusta **native** backing is freestanding / libc-free (see Augusta rules).